As someone living in Europe, the fastest land animal would be the cheetah (Acinonyx jubatus). Cheetahs are native to some parts of Africa but have been introduced to other regions including parts of Europe. They can reach speeds up to 70 mph or 112 km/h.

However, if you're referring to the fastest bird, it's the peregrine falcon (Falco peregrinus). Peregrine falcons are found in many parts of the world, including Europe, and they are known for their incredible diving speed when hunting. They can reach speeds up to 240 mph or 386 km/h during a dive.

Please note that these animals may not be encountered frequently depending on your specific location within Europe.